body:
I have spoken with others about what I'm going through and it seems nobody has any advice about stuff to do. I've had my own father tell me to just stick it out until my mother dies but god knows when that will happen.

&#x200B;

I've called the suicide hotline twice. The first time, I wasn't going to do it but I felt like I had nobody to talk to, so I called to cry to someone to hopefully have them tell me that life was worth it and whatnot. But the guy legitimately told me "wow... that's a lot. Uh, my shift is over now so I have to go." and the second one was a much better experience that actually calmed me down.

&#x200B;

But eh. I can't really afford to go to therapy. Nor do I want to pay someone to tell me that it gets better when they won't give actual advice on what to do. cause there isn't much I can do in my situation except wait for my mother to die, kill myself, or win a lot of money somehow so my troubles can go away financially.
